- Otherwise (1)-(5) follow from the quoted theorem: chi factor, inequality directions, optimisation and normalisation correct; successive fixed-parameter limits, no uniformity in R, degree or theta needed; fixed R ~ 7.6 no restriction. 2 pi (1.2036) = 7.56244.
Auditor's resolution: (a) presentation gap only: the certificate uses rho <= rho_max - 0.02 (finite alpha certified), and H is real-analytic with a simple crossing at rho_max; (b) DERIVATION uses Z_T-conjugation = rho <-> 1 - conj(rho) (its section 0; La l.588-598); (c) o(T) details. No number changes.
